Step 1: Find the Service name
kubectl get services

Step 2: Start port forwarding

On the EC2 instance, run:

kubectl port-forward svc/nginx-demo-my-nginx 8080:80

Keep this terminal running.

You should see:

Forwarding from 127.0.0.1:8080 -> 80
Step 3: Create an SSH tunnel from Windows

Open a new PowerShell window on your Windows laptop.

Run:

ssh -i "C:\Users\Dell\Downloads\iot-project-key.pem" -L 8081:127.0.0.1:8080 ubuntu@ec2-65-0-99-2.ap-south-1.compute.amazonaws.com

Replace YOUR_EC2_PUBLIC_IP with your actual EC2 public IP.

Keep this SSH session open.

Step 4: Open the application

Open your browser on Windows and enter:

http://localhost:8081

You should see the NGINX welcome page.

Congratulations! You have successfully deployed an application using Helm and accessed it from your laptop.

STEP 5: UPGRADE THE HELM RELEASE

Now let's change the number of replicas from two to three.

Run on EC2:

helm upgrade nginx-demo ./my-nginx \
  --set replicaCount=3

This upgrades the existing release using the same chart and overrides the replica count.

##Verify the Deployment:
kubectl get deployments

##Verify the Pods:
Kubectl get pods

You should eventually see three replicas.

##Check the release history:
helm history nginx-demo
helm list
